From 4e32775f4f7a8350b7b793fea6f561994c95b3be Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Angelo Arifi <arifilabs@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 21:37:29 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] moe-cache: heat-protected eviction keeps hot experts resident
 (turboquant tail)

Full pools now evict the LRU expert whose resident hit count is at or below
GGML_*_MOE_CACHE_HOT_USES (default 4) before touching a hotter expert, so
frequently-used experts stay resident. The provider-agnostic half is in
ggml-moe-cache-common.h (+37/-1); the Vulkan provider - the only one this rig
builds - picks it up in 7 lines. CUDA and Metal land unbuilt on the standing
2026-08-18 HQ ruling for off-rig backends (no NVIDIA/Apple hardware here), the
same law lane-154 landed the original cluster under.

Taken at TIP state d14e36827, not as a delta: all four code files were BYTE
IDENTICAL to the reviewed pin 7ebcbb0b6 beforehand, so tip state and the delta
are the same bytes. docs/backend/MOE-CACHE.md was 2 lines BEHIND the pin
(the 1 GiB auto slab-floor paragraph was missing from our copy); taking tip
restores it as well, which is why its numstat reads 6/1 and not 3/1.

FLAG E untouched: 0 rocmfp/turbo/tq3/q2_0_g128/arifi marker hits in the delta.

Taken-from: llama-cpp-turboquant@730cc87ed (+ its doc follow-up cef75bf06)
Origin: taken at tip d14e36827 for the five touched files; nothing else carried
Measured-effect: UNMEASURED here. The source reports +12% TG (soft) / +7.5%
  (auto) on an RTX 5090 with Laguna S-2.1 - a CUDA measurement on hardware this
  estate does not have, quoted, NOT adopted as our number.
